# Build artifacts and fuzzer state.
#
# corpus/: the small seed inputs already committed stay tracked (ignoring does
# not untrack them), but fuzzer-grown corpus files are NOT tracked — they are
# large binary churn that lives on the fuzzing machine. Minimize periodically
# with `cargo fuzz cmin <target>` and sync with rsync.
/target
/artifacts
/coverage
/corpus
Cargo.lock
__pycache__
